+## Generalizability
 
-The same regression with out-of-pocket cost as outcome gives the upper-bound complement:
+The bounds approach applies to any information-provision intervention where:
+1. The externality (fiscal cost, publicly reimbursed expenditure) is separately observable.
+2. More accurate information weakly improves private utility.
 
-$$\beta_A^{OOP} \approx \Delta U^{upper}.$$
+AHL2022 note this framework applies to restaurant hygiene report cards, electricity usage information programs, hospital quality report cards, and similar public-information interventions.
 
-The interaction coefficients $\beta_A^S$ and $\beta_A^N$ are not bounded by this argument directly; they describe how alert-induced avoidance varies with the shock or norm component of exposure. Interpretation of those interactions belongs to the [[ex-ante-ex-post-adaptation]] framework.
